<section class="soft-section"><div class="wrap feature-lead"><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">The long view</span><h2>Is 91% stable, or falling fast?</h2><p>A single health figure has no direction. Pro keeps the long-term record needed to show whether wear is gradual, accelerating, or approaching the point where a replacement deserves planning, and it doesn't start from nothing: the pack's own lifetime extremes and the gauge's last recalibration go back to before you installed the app.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>Lifetime Analyzer for power, temperature, voltage, and charge</li><li>Monthly health and cycle history per device</li><li>Battery runway forecast for Macs</li><li>Smart alerts for unusual wear and charging conditions</li></ul></div><img src="/img/screenshot-history.png" alt="WhatBattery Pro health history and battery runway" width="440" loading="lazy" /></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap feature-lead"><img src="/img/screenshot-charging.png" alt="WhatBattery Pro charging sessions and charger verdicts" width="440" loading="lazy" /><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">Diagnosis with receipts</span><h2>What drained it, and how did the charger perform?</h2><p>Apps are ranked in real watts rather than a unitless energy score. Charging sessions preserve the delivered power, heat, and charger capability, so the diagnosis does not disappear as soon as you unplug. The Sleep tab covers the hours you weren't watching: charge lost overnight, wake reasons, and what's holding the Mac awake right now, honestly, including when a reading can't be trusted.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>Live and historical app power</li><li>Charge-session history</li><li>Charger capability verdict</li><li>Sleep and wake diagnosis</li><li>Thirty-day charging-habit summary</li><li>Threshold and wear-driven alerts</li></ul></div></div></section>

<section class="soft-section"><div class="wrap feature-lead"><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">All your devices</span><h2>Bring the iPhone and iPad into the same record.</h2><p>Read connected-device health over USB or Wi-Fi without installing another app. Pro retains sparse, long-term health and cycle history so the devices do not vanish from view when they disconnect.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>Health, cycles, temperature, voltage, and live power</li><li>Current-session graph</li><li>Long-term monthly health record</li><li>Mac and connected-device history in one tab</li></ul></div><img src="/img/screenshot-idevice.png" alt="WhatBattery Pro showing a connected iPad Air's battery health and a charge session on the live graph, with a picker to switch to the iPhone" width="440" loading="lazy" /></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap feature-lead"><img src="/img/screenshot-accessories.png" alt="WhatBattery Pro accessory history: AirPods level per bud over a month, with the runtime forecast" width="440" loading="lazy" /><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">Before it dies</span><h2>How do you know a keyboard is about to die?</h2><p>A Bluetooth accessory reports a charge level and nothing else: no health, no cycles, no warning. Pro records that level over time and turns it into a forecast, so a dead mouse in the middle of something is a thing you saw coming.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>Level history per accessory, kept for months</li><li>How long is left: days for a mouse, listening time for AirPods</li><li>Roughly how long a full charge lasts</li><li>AirPods tracked per bud and case</li><li>A low-battery alert that fires before it dies, and says how long is left</li><li>Any accessory's level shown in the menu bar</li></ul></div></div></section>

<section class="soft-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center"><span class="section-tag">Reasons to go Pro</span><h2>Forecast, diagnose, explain, track, prove, and know before it dies.</h2><p>Pro groups the deeper features around the decisions they help you make.</p></div><div class="card-grid two">
  <article class="card"><div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">↘</div><h3>Forecast the replacement</h3><p>Measure wear rate, project the window in which a Mac may reach 80% health, and catch a battery that starts ageing faster than its own trend. No projection at all until the history can support one.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/history/">Explore battery runway →</a></article>
  <article class="card"><div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">W</div><h3>Diagnose the drain</h3><p>Rank your apps by live watts, keep the top users over time, and record how every charge performs. Supported MacBook Pro models also identify chargers that are clearly undersized.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/power/">Explore power analysis →</a></article>
  <article class="card"><div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">Z</div><h3>Explain the overnight drain</h3><p>See exactly what happened during the last sleep: charge lost, wake count, wake reasons in plain English, and what's holding the Mac awake right now. Says so honestly when a reading can't be trusted.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/sleep/">Explore sleep diagnosis →</a></article>
  <article class="card"><div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">iP</div><h3>Track every device</h3><p>Read iPhone and iPad batteries from the Mac, then keep monthly health and cycle history beside the Mac's own record.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/iphone-ipad/">Explore connected devices →</a></article>
  <article class="card" id="reports"><div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">PDF</div><h3>Keep the evidence</h3><p>Create a one-page PDF or print report, export the underlying samples as CSV or JSON, and back up long-term health history.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/history/#reports">Explore reports and export →</a></article>
  <article class="card"><div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">BT</div><h3>Know before it dies</h3><p>Watch every Bluetooth accessory's level over time, see how long is left (days for a mouse, listening time for AirPods), and get the warning before it dies, not after.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/accessories/">Explore accessory forecasts →</a></article>
